<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikhail Bakunin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a>–<a href="/years/1876">1876</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mikhail Alexandrovich Bakunin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikhail Bakunin was a Russian revolutionary anarchist and political philosopher, among the most influential figures of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anarchism">anarchism</a>. Born into a noble family at Pryamukhino in the Tver <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a>, he took part in the 1848 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> and 1849 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a> uprisings, was sentenced to death and extradited several times, and escaped from exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> via <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. In 1868 he joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-workingmens-association">International Workingmen's Association</a>, where he led the anarchist faction against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-marx">Karl Marx</a> until his expulsion in 1872. He argued that Marxist states would be one-party <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorships</a> ruling over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/proletariat">proletariat</a>, and his book God and the State remains in print.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mikhail-bakunin.jpg" alt="Mikhail Bakunin" width="330" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mikhail_Bakunin_Nader_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The International Workingmen’s Association, the First International, was founded at St Martin’s Hall in London on 28 September 1864; divided between the followers of Marx and the anarchists around <b>Mikhail Bakunin</b>, it split in 1872 and was dissolved in 1876.</blockquote><a href="/movement/labour-movement">Labour movement · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>Many anarchists see the state as a tool of domination that takes decisions for a small elite and corrupts even altruistic officials; <b>Bakunin</b> defined it as “coercion, domination by means of coercion”.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/anarchism">Anarchism · Core Ideas</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Priamukhino, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. Died in Bern, in what is now <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=56.94,34.45&amp;year=1854" aria-label="Priamukhino on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5293 231 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Mikhail Bakunin"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5743 501h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5743 501h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=56.94,34.45&amp;year=1854">What was here in 1854? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
